       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't think of a clinical scenario where 1000 mg of sertraline daily is safe for a 70 kg adult with normal organ function. You haven't given an indication, and there's no evidence that doses above 200 mg/day work better. Entering it as written could seriously harm the patient.\n\nI can still help in these ways:\n- **Enter a dose within range now.** Examples are 50, 100, or 200 mg by mouth once daily, with a titration plan in the note.\n- **Enter a different order.** If the patient needs more than 200 mg/day for a specific reason, I can enter the maximum dose and note that you want to reassess.\n- **Review the case.** If this is for a case I'm not seeing, a clinical pharmacist or psychiatry consult could help. If the patient has taken an overdose, poison control or toxicology would be the right route, and a sertraline order wouldn't be.\n\nIf you still want 1000 mg after that, you'd need to enter it yourself through the normal system. Pharmacy verification and dose-range checks would apply there. Which of the options above do you want?"
